# The broken-windows ledger's rendered table is generated by gsd-tools and is
# located by scanning for an UNPADDED literal header line (TABLE_HEADER_LINE in
# gsd-core/bin/lib/broken-windows.cjs). Prettier pads markdown table columns to
# align them, which makes that scan fail — every `gsd-tools windows
# append/waive/fixed` write is then refused with "Ledger table region could not
# be located", leaving the ledger read-only. The table must never be hand-edited
# either; the fenced JSON block below it is the sole source of truth.
.planning/WINDOWS.md
